<title>EGYPT: Egyptian trade deficit $810 mln in October.</title>
<headline>Egyptian trade deficit $810 mln in October.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's trade deficit was 2.738 billion pounds ($810 million) in October 1996, against 2.102 billion in September and 2.933 billion in October 1995.</p>
<p>The Central Agency for Public Mobilisation and Statistics, the government statistics office, gave these figures on Monday (all figures in millions of pounds):</p>
<p>			    Oct 1996     Sept 1996     Oct 1995</p>
<p> Imports		   3,706.8	 3,124.8	3,790.0</p>
<p> Exports		     968.5	 1,023.2	  856.5</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>   Oil and products	450.2	   500.3	  354.8</p>
<p>	  Non-oil	    513.7	   500.8	  480.5</p>
<p>	  Re-exports	   4.6	    22.1	   21.2</p>
<p> TRADE DEFICIT	   2,738.4	 2,101.6	2,933.5</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>			    Jan-Oct 1996	 Jan-Oct 1995</p>
<p> Imports		    36,107.5		32,449.1</p>
<p> Exports		    10,371.1		10,322.2</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>   Oil and products	4,719.4		 3,635.1</p>
<p>	  Non-oil	    5,424.5		 6,490.5</p>
<p>	  Re-exports	   227.2		   196.5</p>
<p> TRADE DEFICIT	    25,736.4		22,126.9</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
